<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion. See
         NDA__c.Move_to_Received.quickAction-meta.xml for the full rationale behind finishing this
         change on the review/underwriting objects (2026-08-27) and for why there is no
         <description> element. Underwriting__c carries no record types, so none of these actions
         needs a record-type criterion.

         THE HOP: Underwriting__c.Stage__c sequence is
         Requested -> In Progress -> [approval] -> Approved -> Completed. This action serves
         Requested -> In Progress, gated on Underwriting_Record_Page by
         {!Record.Stage__c} EQUAL 'Requested'.

         🔴 THIS EDIT FIXES A LIVE LATENT DEFECT AS A SIDE EFFECT. The Advance_Stage entry it
         replaces used booleanFilter '1 AND (2 OR 3)' - this repo has MEASURED that a
         parenthesised OR deploys, survives a retrieve, and is then IGNORED BY THE RENDERER (see
         NDA_Record_Page / LOI_Record_Page headers). So the old button very likely rendered at
         EVERY stage including 'In Progress' and the terminal 'Completed', not only at
         'Requested'/'Approved' as intended. This action and Move_to_Completed are pure AND
         chains, each keyed on one exact stage - do not try to "preserve current behaviour" by
         recreating the OR; the current behaviour is itself the bug.

         🔴 NO BUTTON EXISTS FOR In Progress -> Approved, ON PURPOSE. That hop is owned by the
         principal approval process: Underwriting__c.Submit_for_Approval already renders at
         exactly Stage__c = 'In Progress' and is untouched by this change. Adding a stage-advance
         button there would put a principal-approved underwriting one click away from a deal
         driver, bypassing the approval. This also leaves the
         RecordStageAdvanceService.NO_NEXT_STEP_HINTS entry for 'Underwriting|In Progress'
         reachable only through non-UI callers of RecordStageAdvanceController.advance -
         recommended to leave as-is; retiring it is a separate Apex change this admin task does
         not make. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>In Progress</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
